<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 863 million pesos from the secondary market on Wednesday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and one repurchase agreement, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    337 days   23.33 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    183 days   22.38 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     92 days   21.29 pct</p>
<p>The term and maturity of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    413 million	2 days   17.95 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
